# Local secrets for `wrangler dev`. Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored).
#
# This worker deliberately holds no IMAP credential — the sync worker owns it,
# and writes reach that worker over a service binding (#12).
#
# There is nothing to put here for Cloudflare Access either. The gate reads
# `ctx.access`, which the runtime populates and no file can, and the one value
# it compares against — ACCESS_AUD — lives in the repo-root `.env` rather than
# here. This file stays as the place a real secret would go.

# Worth knowing before you reach for `wrangler dev`:
#
# Access is not in front of a local worker, so `ctx.access` is undefined and
# every local request is answered 401. That is the gate failing closed, not a
# bug.
#
# To drive the tools locally as an authenticated caller, put ACCESS_AUD in the
# repo-root `.env` and run `pnpm run dev`. `wrangler dev` follows the same
# redirected configuration `deploy` does, so scripts/deploy-config.mjs will have
# written an `access.dev` block into the generated config — which is what makes
# `ctx.access` appear locally without editing a committed file. Set
# ACCESS_DEV_EMAIL in `.env` to choose the identity it simulates.
#
# Most work on the MCP tools happens through `pnpm run test` / `test:watch`
# instead, which drive the handler directly.
